&#8220;Petroc&#8221; by Archie Thomson (Curtis Brown) Producers: About Premium Content / Bosena Form: TV Genre: Crime Summary: When a charismatic and volatile Cornish outlaw returns home after twelve years in prison, he sets about reclaiming what he believes has been taken from his family, transforming the Penrose's from small-time crooks into a rising criminal power. Set against the wild Cornish coastline, PETROC is a propulsive family crime saga about loyalty, belonging and identity, and the devastating consequences that follow when the past refuses to stay buried.

TWENTY TWO RECOMMENDATIONS &#8220;Do No Harm&#8221; by Polly Findlay (Casarotto Ramsay) Producers: Hinterland Pictures / Fable Pictures Form: Feature Film Genre: Thriller Summary: Anna, a young doctor, accepts a voluntary night shift away from her family on Christmas Eve. When her mentor, Dr. Petersen, is called away, Anna is left in charge of an overstretched maternity ward. With the pressure mounting, she has to make a series of urgent critical decisions way beyond her experience. Just as things seem to be under control, Anna realises that she's made a tiny and very human error that may end up costing a patient her life.

EIGHTEEN RECOMMENDATIONS &#8220;Mrs. X&#8221; by R&#xED;an Smith (Independent Talent Group) Producers: Available Form: TV Genre: Psychological Thriller Summary: When details of her secret affair show up in a student's homework, an English teacher must do battle with a mysterious blackmailer in this cat-and-mouse game that soon escalates to murder. MRS. X is a twisty-turny thriller, where our lead characters &#x2013; a tense-but-warm sister pairing &#x2013; are always racing against the clock, trying to get one step ahead (while always being ten steps behind). The show interrogates whether we have truly thrown off the shackles of conservative thinking, or if the societal need to control others &#x2013; especially women &#x2013; still bubbles under the surface &#x2026;

FIFTEEN RECOMMENDATIONS &#8220;The Trolley Problem&#8221; by Polly Cavendish (Independent Talent Group) Producers: Imaginarium Form: Feature Film Genre: Psychological Thriller Summary: Young married couple Nick and Georgie are involved in a horrific accident in which a stranger dies. Years later, the decisions they made during those fateful moments come back to haunt them.

&#8220;15 Summers&#8221; by Courttia Newland (Dench Arnold) Producers: Joi Productions Form: Feature Film Genre: Drama Summary: Dimes is a successful rapper whose pursuit of fame estranges him from his teenage son, Tristian. When Tristian joins Dimes on tour, father and son are forced into close proximity, exposing resentment, disappointment and misunderstanding. As Tristian witnesses the contradictions of his father's world &#x2013; glamour, violence and chaos &#x2013; Dimes sees the young man his son is. But when a night out turns violent and Tristian is harmed, Dimes finally confronts the life he has chosen. Over one transformative summer, both must decide whether it's too late for them &#x2013; and whether Dimes can put his son before everything. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

