TWELVE RECOMMENDATIONS &#8220;The Lambeth Worm&#8221; by Bec Boey (The Agency) Producers: Joi Productions/BFI Form: Feature Film Genre: Horror Summary: Inspired by a traditional folklore tale from the writer's native Northeast England, The Lambeth Worm tells the story of two young BESEA women who find a small creature in their tower block apartment. After washing it down the sink, the creature takes up residence in the building's pipes. As fear spreads though the apartment block the other inhabitants become increasingly hostile and toxic, and a culture of terror and blame begins to take hold.

