Amazon Prime Video is doubling down on &#8220; The Terminal List &#8221; franchise, with the streamer developing a series based on Jack Carr's prequel novel &#8220;Cry Havoc.&#8221;

&#8220;The Terminal List&#8221; is based on Carr's James Reece novels, while &#8220;Cry Havoc&#8221; follows Reece's father Tom Reece during the latter's time as a Navy SEAL during the Vietnam war. The character of Tom Reece was recently introduced in Season 2 of &#8220;The Terminal List,&#8221; with David Keeley playing the veteran SEAL in four episodes of the series. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Keira Knightley Says ‘It Means Nothing' When Fans Quote ‘Love Actually’ to Her Because She Hasn’t Watched It Since the Premiere: ‘I Don’t Remember It’ Paul Bettany, Asha Banks, Gugu Mbatha-Raw and Colin Firth Team for Feel-Good Comedy 'It's Alright,' Protagonist Launches Sales at AFM (EXCLUSIVE)

"The Terminal List" already has two shows under its umbrella. Including the original series, which stars Chris Pratt as James Reece, Amazon aired the prequel "The Terminal List: Dark Wolf" starring Taylor Kitsch in 2025, with Kitsch reprising the role of CIA operative and former SEAL Ben Edwards. "The Terminal List" originally debuted in 2022, with Season 2 debuting on Oct. 21, 2026. It was recently reported that Pratt would return in &#8220;Savage Son,&#8221; also based on a James Reece novel, though whether it will serve as a third season of &#8220;The Terminal List&#8221; or a spinoff project remains to be seen.

The official logline for &#8220;Cry Havoc&#8221; states:

&#8220;&#8216;Cry Havoc' takes place in 1968 Vietnam and follows Jack Carr's youngest protagonist, Tom Reece, a brash Navy SEAL assigned to the top secret MACV-SOG unit which ran harrowing cross-border operations in Laos. When Tom's Recon Team comes across plans for the upcoming Tet Offensive, it unleashes a chain of events that pulls the young warrior out of the jungles and into the shadows of Cold War espionage.&#8221;

The show is being developed for television by the team behind &#8220;The Terminal List.&#8221; David Digilio, Max Adams, Jared Shaw, and Carr are all developing the show, with Adams and Digilio writing the pilot script. All are executive producers on &#8220;Cry Havoc,&#8221; with Digilio set to serve as showrunner. Digilio developed both &#8220;The Terminal List&#8221; and the prequel series &#8220;The Terminal List: Dark Wolf&#8221; and serves as showrunner on both shows. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

As with &#8220;The Terminal List,&#8221; Antoine Fuqua executive produces with Kat Samick for Fuqua Films, with Pratt executive producing via Indivisible. MRC and Amazon MGM Studios produce.

Fourteen years before his official casting as James Bond , Robert Pattinson expressed interest in playing cinema's most famous secret agent. The actor was speaking to the U.K. online publication Shortlist (via People ) in the summer of 2012, a few months ahead of both his swan song as Edward Cullen in &#8220;The Twilight Saga: Breaking Dawn &#x2013; Part 2&#8243; and the release of Daniel Craig's third Bond movie &#8220;Skyfall,&#8221; when he was asked about becoming the next 007 actor. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

"Yeah definitely, but more like 20 years," Pattinson answered at the time. &#8220;I think there'd be nothing worse than, like, &#x2018;Let's get a fresh-faced Bond!' That would be the worst idea in the world. After Daniel Craig, you have to have some baggage. It would be ridiculous to reinvent [him] as some young posh kid. Or, if [he] was, I'd have to get so tortured in the first few scenes. I'd have to do the first film with one arm or something." Related Stories Paul Bettany, Asha Banks, Gugu Mbatha-Raw and Colin Firth Team for Feel-Good Comedy 'It's Alright,' Protagonist Launches Sales at AFM (EXCLUSIVE) Keira Knightley Says ‘It Means Nothing' When Fans Quote ‘Love Actually’ to Her Because She Hasn’t Watched It Since the Premiere: ‘I Don’t Remember It’

It turns out Pattinson only needed 14 years to agree to sign on as the new James Bond, taking over the franchise after Daniel Craig's exit in &#8220;No Time to Die.&#8221; Pattinson will be the first 007 under the franchise's new owner, Amazon MGM Studios. Denis Villeneuve, who directed Pattinson in &#8220;Dune: Part Three,&#8221; is helming the movie. Pattinson reportedly beat out contenders such as Jack Lowden, Callum Turner, Josh O'Connor and Nicholas Hoult in the final rounds of auditions.

"James Bond is one of the most legendary characters in cinema, and to be entrusted with 007 is the honor of a lifetime," Pattinson said in a statement about his casting as Bond. &#8220;To say this role is a dream come true is an understatement. I couldn't be more excited about this partnership and the work ahead with this fantastic team." blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Villeneuve added in his own statement: "Before anything else, I want to express my deep gratitude to the remarkable actors who joined us on this journey. We were surrounded by extraordinary talent, but there can only be one 007. I am overjoyed to welcome Robert Pattinson as our new James Bond. He has the timeless soul of 007 and brings a spirit that is completely new. I cannot wait to begin."

Amy Pascal, who has produced the "Spider-Man" franchise and several 007 films, and David Heyman, the producer behind the "Harry Potter" series, are producing the new Bond film, with Tanya Lapointe executive producing. The script is by &#8220;Peaky Blinders&#8221; creator Steven Knight.

The Brit List , the platform for emerging British screenwriting talent, has unveiled its 2026 lineup of the best unproduced film and TV scripts from emerging creatives &#x2014; 13 scripts from 13 writers.

Two projects received the highest number of recommendations: Dig for Victory by Gemma Addy, who has worked on the TV drama series Marie Antoinette , and Petroc by Archie Thomson, one of the writers on California Schemin' .

